---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ArrowLeft, LogOut, Mail, ShieldCheck } from "@lucide/astro";
import "@styles/account.css";
---

<BaseLayout active="utilities" title="Utility account | Austin Garrod" description="Sign in to sync your utility saves and manage recovery copies." noIndex privatePage>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero-compact">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Utility accounts</p>
      <h1>Utility account</h1>
      <p>Sign in with an emailed code or Google to sync your utilities. You can also use the utilities without an account.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container account-layout rr-block" data-analytics-private>
    <div>
      <p id="account-status" class="account-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking account availability…</p>
      <div id="account-unavailable" class="account-panel" hidden>
        <h2>Accounts are temporarily unavailable</h2>
        <p>Your utilities and their backup tools still work, and nothing saved on this device has changed.</p>
        <button type="button" class="button" id="account-retry">Try again</button>
      </div>
      <div id="account-signed-out" class="account-panel" hidden>
        <h2 id="account-sign-in-heading">Sign in or create an account</h2>
        <p id="account-google-verification" hidden>Verify this email address to finish connecting Google to your account.</p>
        <form id="account-email-form" class="account-sign-in-form">
          <label for="account-email">Email address</label>
          <input id="account-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254" />
          <button type="submit" class="button primary" id="account-email-submit"><Mail size={17} aria-hidden="true" />Email a sign-in code</button>
        </form>
        <form id="account-code-form" class="account-sign-in-form" hidden>
          <label for="account-code">Six-digit code</label>
          <input id="account-code" name="code" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="one-time-code" pattern="[0-9]{6}" minlength="6" maxlength="6" required aria-describedby="account-code-note" />
          <p id="account-code-note" class="form-note">Enter the code from your email. It expires after ten minutes.</p>
          <button type="submit" class="button primary" id="account-code-submit">Sign in</button>
        </form>
        <div class="account-divider" id="account-sign-in-divider"><span>or</span></div>
        <button id="account-google" class="button account-google" type="button">Continue with Google</button>
        <p class="form-note">Pokémon Binder Tracker and Idle Slayer Companion let you review guest saves before connecting. Radius Map opens your account library when you sign in.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="account-signed-in" class="account-panel" hidden>
        <p class="eyebrow"><ShieldCheck size={16} aria-hidden="true" />Signed in</p>
        <h2 id="account-identity"></h2>
        <p>Open a utility to sync or review its existing saves. Each utility keeps its own progress and recovery copies.</p>
        <h3 class="account-group-heading">Open a utility</h3>
        <div class="account-utility-links">
          <a class="button" href="/utilities/pokemon-binder/">Pokémon Binder Tracker</a>
          <a class="button" href="/utilities/idle-slayer-companion/">Idle Slayer Companion</a>
          <a class="button" href="/utilities/radius-map/">Radius Map</a>
        </div>
        <p id="account-migration-paused" class="form-note" hidden>New save migrations are temporarily paused. Existing local saves remain available.</p>
        <h3 class="account-group-heading account-group-divided">This account</h3>
        <div class="account-actions">
          <button id="account-link-google" class="button" type="button">Connect Google</button>
          <button id="account-logout" class="account-text-button" type="button"><LogOut size={16} aria-hidden="true" />Sign out</button>
          <button id="account-logout-all" class="account-text-button" type="button">Sign out everywhere</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note">Signing out keeps your device’s saved data. Pending changes stay associated with this account.</p>
      </div>
      <section id="account-assistants" class="account-panel" hidden aria-labelledby="account-assistants-heading">
        <div class="account-recovery-heading">
          <h2 id="account-assistants-heading">Connected assistants</h2>
          <a class="text-link" href="/account/assistants/">Set up an assistant</a>
        </div>
        <p id="account-assistants-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <ul id="account-assistants-list" class="account-recovery-list"></ul>
      </section>
      <section id="account-recovery" class="account-panel" hidden aria-labelledby="account-recovery-heading">
        <div class="account-recovery-heading">
          <h2 id="account-recovery-heading">Recovery copies</h2>
          <button id="account-recovery-refresh" class="button compact" type="button">Refresh</button>
        </div>
        <p>Migration and conflict copies stay here until you delete them. Restoring a copy also preserves the version it replaces.</p>
        <p id="account-recovery-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <details id="account-sync-history" class="account-sync-history" hidden>
          <summary id="account-sync-history-summary">Sync checkpoints</summary>
          <p>Each save keeps checkpoints for up to three days with synced changes.</p>
          <ul id="account-sync-history-list" class="account-recovery-list"></ul>
          <button id="account-sync-history-more" type="button" class="button compact" hidden>Show older versions</button>
        </details>
        <ul id="account-recovery-list" class="account-recovery-list"></ul>
      </section>
      <a id="account-return" class="text-link account-return" href="/utilities/"><ArrowLeft size={17} aria-hidden="true" />Back to utilities</a>
    </div>
    <aside class="account-aside">
      <h2>Keep a copy</h2>
      <p>Your utilities’ existing JSON backup and transfer tools remain available. A downloaded backup is useful before moving devices or clearing browser storage.</p>
      <p>Signing into an account cannot find saves in another browser. Open that browser and sign in there, or import its exported backup.</p>
      <p><a href="/account/privacy/">How account data is used</a></p>
      <p><ShieldCheck size={17} aria-hidden="true" />Your data stays separate from other accounts on this device.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <script>
    import "../../utilities/accounts/account-page";
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
